## Purpose

Prove the private-reachability invariant end to end and close bypasses before B259 is marked complete.

## Work

- Build an attack-oriented regression matrix spanning unauthorised authenticated peers, anonymous clients, forged aliases, guessed identifiers, stolen/expired/revoked credentials, replay, recipient/host confusion, malformed input, concurrency, restarts, and mixed versions.
- Cover HTTP, WebSocket, connector, direct CLI, local-vs-remote routing, in-memory/SQLite parity, public/gated/unlisted rooms, and dev-mode boundaries.
- Verify rejected messages never reach inboxes, archives, dead letters, transcripts, wake/injection surfaces, or message-content logs.
- Dogfood against an isolated local relay using canonical tmux helpers; do not run write-capable smoke tests against production.
- Run an independent security review against the exact intended invariant and fix all accepted blocker/major findings.
- Update the evidence ledger with final code symbols and named tests.

## Acceptance evidence

- Fresh explicit builds precede tests; repo-wide forced test counts use the repository's documented anti-false-green procedure and two-thread limit.
- Security review reports no unresolved blocker/major issue.
- Evidence demonstrates both denial of unauthorised first contact and successful deliberately authorised contact.

## Post-B219 audit requirements (from B261)

- Both backends; `/send` + `/send_all` + `/forward`; discovery oracles; zero side effects on reject (inbox, push, stats, content DLQ, archives, wakes).
- Concurrent revoke vs admit under the established lock; restart persistence; migration interruption/mixed versions.
- Keep B219 lifecycle tests green: `test_relay_sqlite_persistent_connection_stress`, `test_relay_sqlite_request_nonce_no_leak_under_load`, `test_relay_sqlite_mixed_ops_on_shared_connection`.
- Design input + seams: `.collab/research/2026-07-22-b261-private-reachability-persistence-reconciliation.md`.

## Prepared attack-evidence requirements

Map every B262 G1–G9 and B259 acceptance row to an exact suite/command before completion. Required integration matrix: both backends; HTTP peer auth; WebSocket subscribe/push; connector outbox/retry; CLI/contact-card flow; direct `/send`; `/send_all`; `/forward`; rooms/rosters; restart/concurrency; fresh/legacy/interrupted/mixed-version migration; tokenless development; zero inbox/push/wake/archive/DLQ/stats/log side effects on rejection; authorised exactly-once control. Co-run final B219 lifecycle tests. Dogfood only against an isolated local relay using canonical tmux helpers. Follow all eight anti-false-green rules in AGENTS.md and preserve exact commands/counts/exit codes in the goal evidence and claim ledger.